        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Footprint plus 6 feet behind, 2 feet either
            side, and a foot above your head once the deck has lifted you.</strong>
            For a full-size machine that is roughly 12 by 7 feet of room and about
            7 foot 10 of ceiling. Tape the outline on the floor and live with it
            for a day before ordering anything.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            If the numbers do not work, change the machine rather than the
            clearance — a
            <a href="/walking-pad-vs-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">walking pad</a>
            solves most small-room cases outright, and the
            <a href="/treadmill-belt-size-guide/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">belt size guide</a>
            explains exactly what a shorter deck costs you.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
